ACC-012 — Decision Support

Document ID: ACC-012
Title: Decision Support
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines Decision Support, the cognitive function through which Atlas communicates engineering conclusions, recommendations, alternatives, and supporting rationale to assist engineering decision-making.

Decision Support transforms Engineering Reasoning and Engineering Capability outputs into actionable guidance while preserving transparency, traceability, and human oversight.

2. Scope

This specification applies to all decision support generated within the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework.

Decision Support may assist with:

Design decisions
Planning decisions
Compliance decisions
Construction decisions
Maintenance decisions
Risk mitigation
Alternative selection
Resource allocation
Engineering approvals
Operational decisions
Strategic engineering planning

This specification defines support for decisions, not autonomous decision-making.

3. Canonical Definition

Decision Support is the structured presentation of engineering conclusions, recommendations, alternatives, confidence, and supporting rationale to assist informed engineering decision-making.

Decision Support assists decision-makers.

It does not replace them.

4. Characteristics

Decision Support SHALL possess the following characteristics.

4.1 Explainable

Decision Support SHALL provide sufficient explanation to justify every recommendation.

4.2 Evidence-Based

Decision Support SHALL be supported by Engineering Evidence.

4.3 Reasoning-Informed

Decision Support SHALL be derived from Engineering Reasoning.

4.4 Context-Aware

Decision Support SHALL be presented within the applicable engineering context.

4.5 Transparent

Decision Support SHALL disclose assumptions, limitations, uncertainties, and confidence where applicable.

4.6 Action-Oriented

Decision Support SHALL assist engineering decision-makers in evaluating feasible courses of action.

4.7 Human-Centric

Decision Support SHALL preserve the authority of qualified engineers and designated decision-makers.

4.8 Traceable

Decision Support SHALL maintain traceability to the Engineering Understanding, Engineering Evidence, and Engineering Reasoning that produced it.

